--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (reproduced from the web source — composition, data, states, i18n)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data hooks : web useCreateIncident (POST /status/incidents + list invalidation) → P1/S8 `IncidentCreating` seam ;
               web useToast (success/error) → the model's published `IncidentFormToast` + the view's toast banner ;
               web useId (label/input associations) → SwiftUI label-for-control + FocusState (title autoFocus).
  Submit     : web handleSubmit → `IncidentFormModel.submit()`: trim title, guard length<3 (toast.error, NO network,
               stay open), else mutateAsync({ title, severity, status, initial_message?, affected_components[] }) →
               toast.success("Incident logged.") + onClose() ; onError → toast.error(err.message ?? 'Failed to log
               incident'). Button "Logging…" + disabled while pending. Re-entrancy guarded.
  i18n keys  : every web literal shipped in the "IncidentForm" table — title "Log an incident"; labels Title / Severity /
               Status / Affected components (+"(comma-separated, optional)") / Initial timeline message (+"(optional)");
               options Minor/Major/Critical + Investigating/Identified/Monitoring/Resolved; prompts; Cancel / "Log
               incident" / "Logging…"; toasts "Title must be at least 3 characters." / "Incident logged." / "Failed to
               log incident". Native-only chrome (still localized): close, offline toast, dismiss, a11y hints. The view
               holds no bare English literal (all via the IncidentFormStrings facade).
  States     : this is a create FORM — the web source has NO data fetch (no useQuery), so the generic loading / empty /
               stale read-states are N/A by parity (no async read source exists to be in them). The form's real states
               ARE reproduced and tested, none hidden: editing (always-rendered fields, never a blank box) / submitting
               ("Logging…", disabled) / validation-error (toast) / submit-error (generic + offline toast = the prompt's
               `error`/`offline` branches) / success (toast + dismiss). Every branch has a preview + a unit test + an
               executed host check.
  Apple HIG  : SwiftUI card dialog (sheet-presentable), native menu Pickers for the selects, TextEditor for the
               multiline message, ProgressView on the in-flight submit, Dynamic Type (token fonts), Reduce-Motion-safe
               animations, VoiceOver labels/hints on every control, decorative icons hidden. iOS 18 / iPadOS 18 (compact
               width stacks the selects + actions) / macOS 15 (AppKit token branches) all compile.

